    <summary>A powerful, cross-platform terminal-based task monitor.</summary>
    <description>
Task Monitor (taskmon) is a powerful, cross-platform terminal-based task monitor that provides
real-time monitoring and management of system performance, active processes, and resource
utilization. Inspired by tools like top, htop and the Windows Task Manager.

### Features
- Real-time process monitoring (CPU, GPU, memory, disk I/O, network I/O, thread counts)
- Advanced process information including module lists, thread states and command-line arguments
- Multi-process selection and termination
- Filtering by process name, username or PID, and flexible column sorting
- Rich system metrics with visual meters
- Keyboard-driven interface with F1-F10 hotkey support
- Built-in themes, layouts and configurable colors
- Native performance using platform-specific APIs

### Package notes
This package installs a self-contained, natively compiled (AOT) single-file executable.
It automatically selects the x64 or ARM64 build to match your machine. The `taskmon`
command is shimmed onto your PATH by Chocolatey.

taskmon does not require elevated permission for system monitoring, however some system
process detail won't be available unless run as Administrator.
    </description>
    <releaseNotes>https://github.com/jchas2/taskmon/releases</releaseNotes>
